{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1229374-1000-rotes","id":1229374,"title":"1000 Rotes","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-06-22T08:40:23-07:00","id":1229374,"title":"1000 Rotes","content":"Let's play a game! List a rote or two, or as many as you want. Be sure to include what sect(s) can use the rote, as well as the spheres required and a basic description of it's effects. Here's a few examples.<br /> <br /> 1. The Golem (Lions of Zion) Life 5, Mind 5, Matter 5: <br /> <br /> The Lion using this rite takes fresh, unused natural minerals and sculpts a human figure out of it. Then, they invoke the name of Yahweh to awaken the golem while writing Hebrew for Truth on it's head.<br /> <br /> 2. Portal Gun (New World Order) Correspondence 3:<br /> <br /> This Technocratic Procedure requires a small, arm-sized machine which some cyborgs use as a prosthetic. The portal is about the size of a person, and can take you anywhere within line of sight.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24271-froggo","name":"Froggo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24271_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-30T08:26:41-07:00","id":1231367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Froggo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1229374-1000-rotes#post1229374\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let's play a game! List a rote or two, or as many as you want. Be sure to include what sect(s) can use the rote, as well as the spheres required and a basic description of it's effects. Here's a few examples.<br /> <br /> 1. The Golem (Lions of Zion) Life 5, Mind 5, Matter 5: <br /> <br /> The Lion using this rite takes fresh, unused natural minerals and sculpts a human figure out of it. Then, they invoke the name of Yahweh to awaken the golem while writing Hebrew for Truth on it's head.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Why would a Golem need Mater 5 or life 5? Those levels are way too high for a Golem, what youre describing is more akin to an entirely new biological life form, not even homunculus needs that much spheres.<br /> <br /> Funny fact though, by rules all you need to make a golem closer to the jewish myth is Spirit 3 and Awaken Spirit rotine. Of course the said golem would be quite weak and perhaps even incapable of locomotion at first, but a golem notheless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24274-menos125","name":"menos125","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"43"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T00:22:20-07:00","id":1231733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>menos125</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1229374-1000-rotes?p=1231367#post1231367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why would a Golem need Mater 5 or life 5? Those levels are way too high for a Golem, what youre describing is more akin to an entirely new biological life form, not even homunculus needs that much spheres.<br /> <br /> Funny fact though, by rules all you need to make a golem closer to the jewish myth is Spirit 3 and Awaken Spirit rotine. Of course the said golem would be quite weak and perhaps even incapable of locomotion at first, but a golem notheless.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Life 5 to give the creation life (to create a new life pattern from nothing), Matter 5 to match the life spell and to make the creation permanent until destroyed. Though I can see a Matter 5/Spirit 3 rote as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/j5vvlqp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/ghw20supporterhiddengaroup\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/n18segp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0v25ewp\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#404040\"><span style=\"font-family:Verdana\">English is not my native language, so i apologize for errors in grammar or spelling.</span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/392-cadmiumcadamium","name":"Cadmiumcadamium","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar392_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"936"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-02T04:14:10-07:00","id":1231757,"title":"","content":"I am not sure why Matter 5 is required in this case either way - depending on the nature of the artificial body it might well be enough to use Matter 2, especially in the classic tale of the Golem being made of clay.<br /> <br /> The permanency of Matter 5 itself is only required for permanent re-shaping of matter without any spell duration. And even then, in this case it's enough to just get 6-7 successes counting towards the duration to make the Golem worthwhile - the permanency that Matter 5 would offer in terms of the shaping kind of becomes obsolete by the fact that the other aspects of teh Golem are still unweavable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-19T11:06:02-07:00","id":1236837,"title":"","content":"I don't think there's need in Life. The golem is like a robot - an intellegence inside of unliving but moving body. So it's Mind 5 to create... wel... mind. And Matter 3 for simple body like living armor or Matter 4 for complex mechanisms such as robots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24212-mesmeroflife","name":"MesmerOfLife","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T12:38:46-07:00","id":1237804,"title":"","content":"3. Trajectory calculations (Correspondence 1, Entropy 1, /Forces 2 or Correspondence 1, Time 1, Forces 1/2): Anyone who has an idea of how to make sniper shots can tell you that there is a lot of maths involved there, but with this rote you can elevate that yo a new level maximizing the reach of any firearm (especially rifles) and even shoting through walls/obstacles. This rote is usually used by technocratich spec-ops and the most adventurous Sons of Ether, but is not unheard of some mages from cabals with more mystical inclinations like Order of Hermes or the Euthanatoi using numerology with the same results.<br /> <br /> Effect: Using Correspondence (to know exacly where and how far the objetive is) Time (to know how long the shoot will is) Forces and Entropy (to know the forces that will affect the bullet like gravity, wind speed, etc until the objective) you can make any shot at base difficulty no matter how long it is while is in the possible ballistic trajectory of the weapon with 2 succeses (3 if there is no line of sgiht wit the objective. Aditional succeses can drop the difficulty). Forces 2 can use aditional succeses to add succeses to the shoot or to ignore obstacles maximizing penetration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24126,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24126-bartimeo","user":"Bartimeo","date":". 07-23-2018, 03:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24126-bartimeo","name":"Bartimeo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24126_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-22T23:59:53-07:00","id":1237904,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bartimeo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1229374-1000-rotes?p=1237804#post1237804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. Trajectory calculations (Forces 1/2, Correspondence 1, Time 1, Entropy 1): Anyone who has an idea of how to make sniper shots can tell you that there is a lot of maths involved there, but with this rote you can elevate that yo a new level maximizing the reach of any firearm (especially rifles) and even shoting through walls/obstacles. This rote is usually used by technocratich spec-ops and the most adventurous Sons of Ether, but is not unheard of some mages from cabals with more mystical inclinations like Order of Hermes or the Euthanatoi using numerology with the same results.<br /> <br /> Effect: Using Correspondence (to know exacly where and how far the objetive is) Time (to know how long the shoot will is) Forces and Entropy (to know the forces that will affect the bullet like gravity, wind speed, etc until the objective) you can make any shot at base difficulty no matter how long it is while is in the possible ballistic trajectory of the weapon with 2 succeses (3 if there is no line of sgiht wit the objective. Aditional succeses can drop the difficulty). Forces 2 can use aditional succeses to add succeses to the shoot or to ignore obstacles maximizing penetration.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not only a great root, but also one of the mostrar common. Many of my gunfights are based on this. Nonetheless, I dont use time in this root. We dont even put in Forces If we are talking about making a bullet turn corners.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6851-sangros","name":"Sangros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6851_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-07-23T00:29:04-07:00","id":1237906,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sangros</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1229374-1000-rotes?p=1237904#post1237904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Not only a great root, but also one of the mostrar common. Many of my gunfights are based on this. Nonetheless, I dont use time in this root. We dont even put in Forces If we are talking about making a bullet turn corners.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks! ^^<br /> <br /> It's true that with Entropy to know &quot;random&quot; variables Time and Forces is a little overkill... I will edit for a Correspondence 1, Entropy 1 OR Correspondence 1, Time 1, Forces 1 (Forces 2 to shoot through walls in both variants)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24126,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24126-bartimeo","user":"Bartimeo","date":". 07-23-2018, 03:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24126-bartimeo","name":"Bartimeo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24126_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T06:32:48-08:00","id":1427452,"title":"","content":"Kinda sus (Virtual Adepts) Mind 2 <br /> <br /> Transfers all suspicion against the user to an innocent bystander. Developed by some Virtual Adept who got stuck on a Void Engineer spaceship.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1235-eadee","name":"Eadee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1235_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"209"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T08:57:42-08:00","id":1427461,"title":"","content":"<i>Respect for whome it is due </i>Mind 3<br /> This Procedure of the Technoracy is a transfer of emotions and thoughts of sympathy from one person to another. That is, (for example) an Acolyte of a mystic Mage might find their sympathy for the mystic rapidly sapped as it is replaced by respect and sympathy for the Technocrat performing this Procedure. The Procedure is relatively obvious when it happens, and a person can very well snap of it (given time), but in a tense situation, it can make all the difference for a Technocrat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-06-2020, 01:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-06T12:35:22-08:00","id":1427478,"title":"","content":"<i>What's mine is mine</i> Correspondence 2<br /> This Rote developed by Ecstatics shifts around any technically illegal substances around the person's clothes while she or he is being mundanely searched for them. The end result is that the drugs are not found, though they might have shifted around to different pockets. It has to be said that no self-respecting Ecstatic would attract enough attention to be searched by the police while just going around the city. However, there are some situations when searches are more likely to happen - like at music and entertainment festivals. Even if the occasions the Rote is useful are few and far between, knowing it is a point of pride for many drug using CoE Mages.<br /> Some Tradition Mages have expressed interest in this Rote potentially being able to hide other items from a search, but no variants have been developed so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-09T06:27:43-08:00","id":1427854,"title":"","content":"A bunch of rotes used by my Wu Lung character from years back by the name of Hu. Hu used his position in the Celestial bureaucracy to exert appropriate authority upon reality and used martial arts, energy work, alchemy and craft magic as well. Sadly he died when a mummy threw him at, and nearly through, another character. Forgive the cheesy names of the effects. I was aiming for something that sounds like it has been translated effectively word for word from a chinese language without any attempt to translate it into what we would say in English. I was also aiming for some of the oldey-timey kung fu movies feel that Hu was raised on.<br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Dance of the 8 Steps</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Mind *, Correspondence *, Forces *</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This rote, almost always coincidental is virtually indistinguishable from Hu's martial arts. With it he compartmentalises his mind, creating one train of thought for each combatant in the fight. Each mind then observes the combat using correspondence and forces magic to precisely gauge where his opponents are, where they are moving and how fast. This allows him an almost preternatural ability to avoid his enemies blows and to strike them in turn, slipping past blocks and attacking into dodges. In practical terms he enjoys a -1 on the difficulty to dodge and to attack when in combat for each success (will probably need a success for duration too). Attackers who he is unaware of are not subject to this as he won't have created a mind track for them. He can monitor one opponent for each success on his casting roll.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Martial Arts - Hu takes a sharp breath in and exhales while stepping through the 8 positions of combat taught by the Kuei Lung Chuan making note of each combatant.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Death of Demons</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Prime **</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Demons (such as vampires, wraiths, fallen magi, shapeshifters, etc) are notoriously hard to kill with normal weapons. Therefore Hu enchants all his weapons with this effect, renewing it weekly. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Alchemy - Hu washes the weapon in a mix of prepared oils and spring water and then burns a piece of paper with the kanji for ruin and death under the blade so that its smoke is absorbed into the weapon.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Surprising Powder that Engenders Great Confusion</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Mind **</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This rote is triggered by flinging a sachet of quickly torn paper full of powder into the face of an enemy. The powder is absorbed through the skin and particularly through the lungs and eyes and greatly confuses the target, leaving them briefly wondering what's going on, where they are and what they were just doing. This typically takes a few rounds to wear off at which point the target manages to make enough sense of their surroundings that they can function again, but until that time they are effectively out of the picture, only taking actions to preserve their life such as dodging attacks and staying away from obviously dangerous places like the edges of rooftops or cliffs. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Alchemy - Hu prepares the powder in advance, combining a number of ingredients such as beach sand, grave dirt and pepper. This powder is then magically fired in a kiln and mixed with ash from burnt pieces of paper covered with prayers and supplications to Hu's ancestors to muddle the thoughts of his foes. The powder is poured into sachets and when Hu throws these he does not consider that he is doing magic at all. As far as he is concerned, the magic happens at home.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Healing Tonic of the Phoenix Empress</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Life **</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">As a warrior, Hu fully expects to be injured in the line of duty. Luckily his old cabal included a Phoenix Empress Wizard who taught him some of the healing arts. This rote involves mixing and consuming a tonic that mends bone and knits flesh. Its effects are vulgar if the injury was obvious but can be coincidental if the wound was not visible (even broken ribs can be put down to &quot;nasty bruises&quot;). Hu can make these tonics for himself but is not yet skilled enough to heal others through his alchemy.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Alchemy - Hu prepares a tonic from the 5 elements, mixing distilled water, rich loam, pure iron (usually filings) and burning them together using pure cedar wood. This renders down to a murky green liquid which is kept in a bottle or vial marked with a Fu (Paper charm) depicting the kanji for good health and wholeness. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Jackie Chan's Training Montage</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Life ***</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Much to the dismay of his master, who calls this rote </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><i>Earthen Dragon Spirit Body, </i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Hu insists that it more accurately should be called Jackie Chan's Training Montage as that is what it so closely mimics. This is a rote of self improvement, using extreme training methods such as lifting heated cauldrons with ones forearms, repeatedly slapping hot sand, training for hours and hours on the plum blossom stumps, performing 1000 press-ups over lit joss sticks and other over the top exercises. Performed over a week it can permanently raise physical attributes. The exercises used are dependent on the attribute raised. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Extreme training techniques. This also requires expenditure of xp to make the change permanent but only half what it would usually cost (i.e. it is the better body rote).</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Leap of the Celestial Tiger Lord</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Forces **</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">As the Book of Crafts, page 134.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This spell lets Hu engage in Crouching Tiger, Hidden Dragon style acrobatic leaps covering 20 feet per success. Hu generally doesn't go all out, jumping only as far as needed and often only using it to reach a handhold from which to pull himself up rather than making the extra five feet and falling foul of paradox.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Martial Arts - Hu take a deep breath and leaps at the same time as shouting a Kiai.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Deadly Tiger Claw Attack</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Life ***</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">With this brutal move, Hu strikes his target with a flurry of tiger claw attacks, striking directly at one or more of their vital organs which is very badly damaged, usually killing them but certainly putting the target out of action and into great pain. This is a life attack that does two levels of lethal damage for every success after the first (which needs to be expended to affect someone other than Hu). In addition, since this is delivered as part of a martial arts attack, it needs to hit and does normal tiger claw attack damage. Both sets of damage are soaked separately.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Martial Arts - Hu attacks with a flurry of tiger claw attacks shouting a kiai with each one.</span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Ten trapped Thunders</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Forces **</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This handy effect can be used to empower a weapon with a forces effect but requires a source of energy. The weapon must be touched (or nearly so) to a source of energy such as a fire, electrical cable, moving car, etc and the energy is sucked into a trap around the weapons striking surface. The energy discharges on the next strike of the weapon which must be during the next round, any longer and the energy dissipates harmlessly. This effect is a useful way to perform forces counter magic, allowing Hu to catch fireballs or lightning bolts and use them himself. He can even use it against physical attacks, blocking the attack and stealing the kinetic energy to deliver back on his own strike. Unless there is a very good reason, the spell deals normal forces damage, but requires a successful attack roll. The form of the energy might have secondary effects, fire does aggravated damage to vampires, kinetic might knock someone off their feet, electricity might short out electronics, etc.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Hu adopts a receiving stance and holds the weapon boldly in front of him before either blocking or striking the energy source as appropriate and inhaling sharply. He then exhales sharply with a kiai when delivering the strike. </span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><b>Incapacitating Acupuncture Meridian Strike</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Life ***</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Hu makes a precise strike with an acupuncture needle, slipping it into a vital meridian and forcing his own yang chi violently through it to disrupt the targets chi flows. This has the effect of paralyzing the target. The paralysis is immediately cancelled if the needle is removed. This is a difficult move to pull off and requires 3 successes on an attack roll with either martial arts or melee. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Attack with an acupuncture needle and a moment\u2019s concentration to disrupt the chi flow.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Obedient Chi Flow Technique</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Mind **</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">With access to a targets meridian points and a set of acupuncture needles, Hu can manipulate the targets chi flow to make them feel various emotions and elicit certain behaviours. His most commonly used trick is to render a target compliant and amenable to requests. With the needles arranged just so, the target becomes very obedient, obeying requests and answering questions to the best of their ability. Note that this changes their inclination, it doesn\u2019t force the behaviour. A target could resist if they really wanted to, but unless the request is obviously self destructive or threatens something they love, they will comply. For this reason it is best to use this to aid interrogation, rather than to replace other methods. To access all the relevant meridians the target must be restrained somehow and their body must be mostly accessible. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: This effect requires a restrained target, a set of acupuncture needles and to get a good effect, some gentle and sympathetic questioning. </span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Puissant Mandarin Sits at his Desk</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Mind *</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This is a very popular rote amongst the Wu Lung. With it active, a Dragon wizard can perform small miracles of administration quickly and accurately. Distractions fade away, numbers come trivially easy to work with and data can be processed, sorted and handled logically and reliably. So popular is this rote that most Wu Lung exams (of which there are many) assume that this rote will be in effect and are hence nearly impossible to pass without such aid. To get \u201cinto the groove\u201d as Hu has it, he must put himself in the mindset of the ancient mandarins of old. This requires a writing desk, appropriate clothing (Hu uses mandarin robes, but office wear should suffice although he has not tried it yet) and the imbibing of a certain tonic, brewed from ingredients linked to clarity, thought, harmony and bureaucracy. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci: Mandarin robes, a writing desk, alchemical tonic and the paperwork that needs processing.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Iron Shirt Technique</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Life ***</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This common combat rote is unobtrusive, useful and handy for ambushes. Once cast, it provides lethal soak equal to the casters stamina. Hu casts the rote via a series of kata focused around bringing his yin chi to the surface of his skin, and deep breathing exercises to lock it in place. Hu is generally a yang driven person so he finds this rote slightly distasteful, but cannot deny its usefulness. In more dangerous times, Wu Lung who might reasonably expect trouble would cast this every morning before leaving the safety of their compounds.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Kuei Lung Chuan katas and deep breathing exercises</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Divine Strike of Angered Ancestors</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Forces ***, Prime **</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This deadly attack uses forces magic to force extreme amounts of kinetic energy into an existing attack. With a cry out to his ancestors for aid and a quick exhalation of chi, Hu channels this energy into an unarmed, melee or thrown attack. This rote does normal forces damage on top of whatever damage the attack would normally have done, making it much harder to soak (i.e. the two damages are added together).</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Shout to his ancestors and a chi expulsion combined with a strike.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Furious Parry</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Forces **</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">With a flury of furious parries, Hu deflects a number of arrows, thrown weapons or even bullets, one per success. They deflect close to him as if parried. Thanks to martial arts movies, most people are willing to believe this when performed against thrown weapons or arrows as long as there are less than five or so. When used against more than that or against bullets, it is clearly vulgar.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Martial arts, needs a weapon like a spear or sword</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Harmonious Hearth Suitable to Honouring Ancestors</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Mind **, prime *</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This effect makes a room or building feel soothing and harmonious. This doesn\u2019t interfere with many emotions but will make it somewhat less likely that people will argue, worry or fight and more likely that people will enjoy each others company, be at peace and find satisfaction in the completion of even trivial tasks. Hu likes to cast this on his flat, making it a place where he can happily practise his art without worrying about things that really aren\u2019t important. </span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Feng shui consisting of placement of furniture and fittings.</span></span><br /> <br /> <b><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Quietly Reverential Place of Reflection</span></span></b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Mind **, prime *</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">This Feng Shui effect uses an uncluttered layout, furniture perpendicular to dragon lines and items of reverence such as funerary jars, calligraphy of noble sentiments and genealogical tablets to create an area that induces those within it to conduct themselves with dignity, reverence and righteousness. Places under this effect can exhibit the same feeling as a cathedral, the desire to talk only in whispers and abide in silent reflection. While violence is possible within such a space (as the effect is mild and subtle), its more likely that someone wishing violence to one within would enter, then leave again and wait for their foe to exit so as not to disturb others.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">Foci</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">: Feng shui consisting of placement of furniture and fittings.</span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4249-gribblethemunchkin","name":"gribblethemunchkin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"94"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T05:39:02-08:00","id":1428588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>gribblethemunchkin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1229374-1000-rotes?p=1427854#post1427854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A bunch of rotes used by my Wu Lung character from years back by the name of Hu.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are some nice Rotes. I especially like <b>Pussaint Mandarin Sits at His Desk</b>, <b>Harmonious Hearth Suitable to Honouring Ancestors, and Quietly Reverential Place of Reflection</b>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T10:40:25-08:00","id":1428618,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>24. <u><b>Talking on the Dancefloor</b></u></u> (Hollow Ones) Spirit 1, Prime 2, Mind 3 + possibly Correspondence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">It allows normal conversation between every Awakened individual in a noisy environment like for instance a club or concert. In addition it also nullifies any language barriers between these mages.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T12:48:57-08:00","id":1428641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Malkavian87</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1229374-1000-rotes?p=1428618#post1428618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><u>24. <u><b>Talking on the Dancefloor</b></u></u> (Hollow Ones) Spirit 1, Prime 2, Mind 3 + possibly Correspondence 2</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#383838\"><span style=\"font-family:-apple-system\"><span style=\"font-size:14px\">It allows normal conversation between every Awakened individual in a noisy environment like for instance a club or concert. In addition it also nullifies any language barriers between these mages.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>A characterful Rote, but what are the Spirit 1 and Correspondence 2 needed for?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T12:51:04-08:00","id":1428644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1229374-1000-rotes?p=1428641#post1428641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A characterful Rote, but what are the Spirit 1 and Correspondence 2 needed for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correspondence 2 for being able to hear someone from the other side of the building?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12952-accelerator","name":"Accelerator","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-16T13:08:07-08:00","id":1428649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1229374-1000-rotes?p=1428641#post1428641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A characterful Rote, but what are the Spirit 1 and Correspondence 2 needed for?</div> </div> </div> </div>Prime 2, Spirit 1 is what it is needed in M20 to detect an Awakened Avatar. Correspondence cause you quite likely don't have line of sight with every possible mage at the venue.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T07:20:49-08:00","id":1428749,"title":"","content":"Couldn't it be just Mind 3 with the possibility of Correspondence 2, and be able to be used in regard to any person, not just another Mage? Possibly with Forces 2 or Prime 2 needed to mute the conversation for other persons. (Prime 2 cause I think Prime should be able to affect phenomena like sound or scent.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 12-17-2020, 10:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-17T16:24:31-08:00","id":1428814,"title":"","content":"This rote came up in my game for the express purpose of a large group of mages (who didn't necessarily know each other) having a meeting in a loud public venue. So this rote is simply tailored to a very specific circumstance.If one had a clear idea of which individuals should or shouldn't be part of the conversation, one would indeed require less spheres.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2198-malkavian87","name":"Malkavian87","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2198_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-12-18T10:50:51-08:00","id":1428881,"title":"","content":"<b>Decipher Notes</b> [Mind 3] This Procedure of the New World Order requires notes - which can be handwritten, printed, or digital - of a person. Using the notes as a focus, the Technocrat locks on the person in question and glimpses understanding of the notes, including overcoming any ciphers used. More successes scored result in a greater amount of information. This Procedure is almost always Coincidental - after all, a lot could be guessed from a few pages somebody left behind. This Procedure can be used from afar with added Correspondence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-24-2021, 01:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-08T10:51:54-08:00","id":1438593,"title":"","content":"<b>Form of the Succubus </b>[Life 5] The Mage assumes the alluring and beautiful form of a mythological temptress. (Or tempter - the Mage can opt to assume the form of an Incubus) Her body is made shapely and attractive to an impassible degree, her feet end in cloven hooves, nails become more akin to talons, wings sprout from her back, and horns grow from her head. Despite these changes the Mage is still recognizable to those who know her. She gains three dots to spend between Social Attributes per success in this Rote. With Prime 3 added, Attributes can exceed scores of 5. This form lasts for a scene. With Prime 2 and Forces 3 added, flight is possible. Nowadays, this Rote is almost always Vulgar. Whether the Mage becomes a Succubus or an Incubus is their own choice - it is not predisposed to the Mage's sex or gender.<br /> <br /> Obviously, this Rote is very useful for improving the carnal matters of the Mage. Unfortunately, using this Rote among the Traditions and the Technocracy certainly creates grounds for a lengthy and extensive investigation into the Mage, if not for outright accusations of Infernalism. On the other hand, it is extremely useful for a Demonologist as an aid in negotiations and confrontations with beings from below.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 03-20-2021, 06:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T07:51:24-08:00","id":1439168,"title":"","content":"<b>Grab a Dealer </b>[Correspondence 3] This refinement of <b>Filter All-Space</b> seeks out a dealer of illegal psychoactive substances. No matter whether they are a seedy part-timer peddling weed on streets, or a dealer of cocaine selling to high-class clients, the Magick of this Rote breaks through space to home in on their position and make them known to the Mage. This Rote is obviously the keepsake of many Ecstatics, who teach it to those in the Traditions who show honest desire and aptitude. Technocrats - from the Syndicate and the Progenitors - each have their own Hyperscience variant.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 03-11-2021, 11:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:38:24-08:00","id":1439186,"title":"","content":"<b>Metal Check</b> [Matter 1] This Rote scans the target person for any firearms she or he might have. More successes give an indication of type, whether they are loaded (and with what), and any deficiencies, idiosyncrasies, or enhancements (including magickal) that the firearms might have.<br /> Technocrats from the Syndicate are known for using this Rote often; not necessarily because they worry about guns, but cause they respect persons who pack the heat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 03-11-2021, 03:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-11T08:43:08-08:00","id":1439187,"title":"","content":"<b>Perceive Higher Paranoia </b>[Mind 2 or Mind 3] This Procedure of the New World Order is a superb tool that allows a Technocrat to read thoughts and feelings of persons in regard to perhaps one of the most valuable kinds of information - the thoughts of a person has in regard to the New World Order itself. As a focus for this Procedure, a conversation needs to be struck with the target on the topic of conspiracies, plots, worries etc. The smallest idiosyncrasies in a person's speech and behavior provide the Technocrat with leverage through which she or he accesses the target's mind in regard to the NWO, using a specialized apparatus.<br /> The functionality of this Procedure can, at request, be included in various Hypertechnological Foci used by Technocrats of the NWO.<br /> <br /> The Mind 3 version allows for more distinct information to be learned, while the Mind 2 version scans the target for fleeting and relatively vague impressions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-24-2021, 01:20 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-12T05:53:25-08:00","id":1439429,"title":"","content":"<b>Psychiatric Tracking</b> [Correspondence 2] - Progenitors sometimes replace (with aid of the NWO if needed) psychiatric medication with slightly altered versions of the pills. These substances, if ingested for at least a week or two, give Progenitor Technocrats a Correspondence Link to the person.<br /> While virtually no Tradition Mage would willingly take psychiatric medication, this Procedure is invaluable for influencing (and experimenting on) members of the Masses.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 07-24-2021, 01:22 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-03-14T11:20:39-07:00","id":1439853,"title":"","content":"<b>Seek out the Big Fish </b>[Correspondence 3] - this Procedure of the Syndicate locates persons who are in charge of and are profiteering from unlawful activities which are part of the so called criminal underworld. The Hyperscience behind this Procedure works by following the trail of laundered money, violence, and broken laws that such figures leave behind them. The focus for this Procedure includes questioning victims of crimes, as well as the local gangsters and made men, and analyzing police records; and then inputting the gathered data into technocratic devices.<br /> Some Mages outside of the Syndicate have claimed that they too can perform such a Correspondence search, but it has to be noted that Syndicate's affinity with both organized crime and money makes this Procedure more efficient than the efforts of other Technocrats and Mages.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 03-14-2021, 02:54 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-18T10:43:13-07:00","id":1464393,"title":"","content":"<b>Catch the Song </b>[Prime 1 or Entropy 1] - this simple Rote pioneered by Ecstatics divines the title and the author of a song (or another piece of music) the Mage is currently listening to. Though simple to cast, some Ecstatics have been known to tire themselves out or suffer Paradox Backlashes after they used this Rote again and again at clubs or raves. The Syndicate does have an Adjustment which achieves the same result through principles of Enlightened Science.<br /> <br /> This Rote requires more success if the title and author of the piece of music somehow became unknown, with just the melody and the words being passed on.<br /> If the author at the time of composing remained anonymous, then this Rote will not inform the Mage who the author is or was. If a piece of music was created under a pseudonym or an alias, then this is what will be known. Likewise, if the author-given title of a piece of music is generally unknown, then it cannot be divined; only information known publically is provided by this Rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-19T10:54:11-07:00","id":1464523,"title":"","content":"<b>Perceive the Hourglass</b>[ Time 1 or Time 2] - This Rote allows a Mage to sense how much time has elapsed since the start of an event or activity, and when it has started. The Time 2 version allows gives a glimpse of how long an event will last, and when it will end. This can be used for simple activities like cooking or cleaning up a room, or for complex events like conferences, university lectures, or parties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-19-2021, 01:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T10:12:16-07:00","id":1464595,"title":"","content":"<b>Track Belongings </b>[Correspondence 1 or 2, Matter 1] - This Rote scans the nearest surroundings (the size of a drawer, a room, or a house, depending on the amount of success) for items belonging to a specific person. An important item belonging to the person in the recent past has to be used as a focus for this Effect. This Rote can be tuned to look for all sorts of items - these of mundane utility, of specific type or size, of a particular degree of importance etc. With enough success, particular items (keys to a car, a specific book, favorite writing implement) can be detected. There is also the option for discovering all nearby items belonging to the person.<br /> This Rote is very useful in saving time while searching a place and when looking for hidden or misplaced items.<br /> <br /> Using Correspondence 1 in this Rote allows for sensing items in the nearest vicinity (at most an area around the size of a house), while the Correspondence 2 variant allows for use of the Rote while scrying on distant location.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-21-2021, 12:42 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T16:32:21-07:00","id":1464659,"title":"","content":"<b>Mystic Pardon</b> [Mind 3] Offer a guilt ridden person an excuse for a misdeed, claiming it was a supernatural or mystical force that pushed them to do it (Manipulation + Subterfuge). If they accept the excuse, even if only outwardly, the Mage casts the effect, rendering them more susceptible to the influencing Magick that they accepted as an explanation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T17:01:56-07:00","id":1464662,"title":"","content":"<b>Karmic Decoy</b> [Life 4, Entropy 3] This rote would be used by a conscientious Life Mage who has extended their lifespan and needs a new identity. The Mage and a willing target swap appearances and the Mage takes on the liabilities of the other. Example, the target is wanted for a murder they committed. The Mage turns themselves in as the target and stands trial, with the advantage of not sharing the fingerprints or genetic markers of the real person. They must work to atone for the crime in some other way, but thereafter have the use of the target's identity. Spell can be cast as a ritual to get enough successes to make the change permanent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T17:18:47-07:00","id":1464664,"title":"","content":"<b>Philosophers' Caffe </b>[Time 4, Correspondence 4, Mind 3] Enter a dream of a gathering in a coffee house with scientists and philosophers from different time periods.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T22:33:52-07:00","id":1464826,"title":"","content":"<b>Perceive Lies of the Past</b> [Entropy 1, Time 2] - Now, a person might be honest about a topic in a particular situation, to a specific person...but what is the guarantee that she or he has not lied or misled others in the past? When there are such doubts, this Rote performs two functions - first, it checks whether a person statement is truthful. Second, it reaches out into the past and gives the Mage a cursory but intense glimpse (filtered through the Mage's Paradigm and Foci) of whether the person was honest about this topic in the past. The casting Mage can control where and how far into the past she reaches, and choose which conversations she wants to divine with Entropy 1.<br /> The Rote tends to provide very scarce information about the past situations - it is focused on checking the degree of honesty in regard to a topic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T06:10:26-07:00","id":1464863,"title":"","content":"Some Nephandi rotes from an old antagonistic nephandi cabal i ran. Naturally they're all bloody awful to descretion is advised.heavy usage of mind.<br /> <br /> Summon 'Satan' Spirit 2 correspondance 2<br /> A nasty little rote planted in the Hollow one community by a Fallen member, the spell is a trap designed to ensare the naive and unseasoned. Theorectically the spell is designed to summon the devil in a context were he/it is unable to harm you. In practice it turns the user into a flare for Spectre's, Banes, Demonic entities and whatever else is nearby. What happens next is up to the GM and the relative power of the poor sap who thought she could call the Devil and control it. The spell itself is simple enough drawing an inverted pentagram in blood (any blood will suffice) place the candles around the points in a holy place at midnight and simply call for satan in a suitable dramatic way. The 'ward' is a red ribbon wrapped around your waist.....it does not work.<br /> <br /> Reverse gaslight Quithlopic mind 4/optional entropy 2/Correspondance 2<br /> An insidious Nephandic spell. The Nephandi supresses a trauma memory in the victim, preferably one which has been resolved and then over a period of time the memory of the event slowly re-emerges. The intent is to undo the years of growth and healing by dragging the victim back to initial trauma of the event. It also damages the victims perception of reality by briefly creating a false more pleasant perception against reality. The ritual requires acquiring a mirror from the victims house smashing it, repairing it and smashing it again. Preferably with some sort of additional sympathetic link included. With entropy you can build in a contingency to trigger the break down and correspondence allows it to be done from a distance.<br /> <br /> &quot;somethings in here with us.&quot; Quithlopic Mind 2 forces 2.<br /> A simple defensive ward designed to scare of sleepers or simply put people on edge. The spell simply amplifies bangs, creaks and groans in an area and combined them with a mind effect to ellavate fear. All that's required is a simply glympth drawn somewhere in area you wish to cast it in.<br /> <br /> Such sights to show you Quithlopic Correspondance 2 Spirit 2, mind 1<br /> This spells opens up a direct line of telepaphic link with the Nephandis patrons and a target, communication is not the aim here. The ultimate objective is massive psychic assault. The caster must had either one eye missing of a third eye hole carved somewhere into their flesh. Damage is bashing but derangements and extreme spiritual corruption are common side effects. Victims must role Diff 6 stamina+Arete test not to black out.<br /> <br /> &quot;The Caul for all&quot; Mind 5, Quithlopic optional spirit 3 and life 4<br /> Somewhat frustrated by slow rate of sleeper corruption, Nephandic magus Steven betruger built a psuado caul to hot box sleeper moral degeneration. The structure/foci itself can vary a great deal in terms of design-sometimes it's a torture box box or an back alley operating theatre or even a room fully of acolytes catering to you every desire or anything the Nephandi can think of to encourage you to be the best you can be. but the ultimate objective is to warp sleepers into more twisted individuals. Typically rather than re-writting the personality the structure is designed to emphasize and unlock the darker aspects of a sleepers personality: hidden and shameful desires, illogical views, personal fears etc and incorperartes them into the psyche at the same time the stunting and minimising the more noble aspects of a sleeper. The person may not necessarily become a Nephandic acolyte (in fact the creator explicitly avoided recruiting from subjects-typically just releasing them back into the wild....a nice and subtle push towards descention) but they're certainly a lot more sympathetic to Nephandic world views afterward<br /> the Life allows for increasingly dramatic body alterations to better suit the new you, Vanity corrupted individuals or may be extremely beautiful, violence junkies may enjoy increased strength, predators may enjoy a lack of fingerprints and so on more drastic changes have been seen but often result in pattern bleeding.<br /> By adding spirit to effect a Bane may be attached to the host for a quick source of shock troops.<br /> <br /> Victims of the effect are genrally quite 'content' with the new them and the process is described as extremely pleasent. Naturally individuals of strong moral character may resist with varying degress of sucesss.<br /> <br /> I'll try and dig up the counter wrotes the Cabal came up with to fight these scumbags.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-25-2021, 03:29 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T05:39:00-07:00","id":1465002,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1229374-1000-rotes?p=1464863#post1464863\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some Nephandi rotes from an old antagonistic nephandi cabal i ran.</div> </div> </div> </div>Out of interest - did you assign them to any of the Nephandi factions? And did you use Widderslaintes? (and if yes, which Essence(s) ?)<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Swallow the Lies and Cough Up the Truth </b>[Entropy 1, Mind 2 or 4] - This Rote checks a statement for truthfulness and honesty. If the statement turns out to be false, the affected person admits it to the Mage, and then is influenced to tell the truth. The number of successes indicates how extensive the admission is, and how substantial the honest statement will be. The Mind 4 variant allows the Mage to ask a question or two, and the targeted person is compelled to elaborate further in regard to the statement or topic.<br /> <br /> If this Rote is used and the statement turns out to be honest, then the casting Mage suffers a strong but brief headache as the Mind Magick element fizzles out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T16:56:06-07:00","id":1465064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1229374-1000-rotes?p=1465002#post1465002\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Out of interest - did you assign them to any of the Nephandi factions? And did you use Widderslaintes? (and if yes, which Essence(s) ?)<br /></div> </div> </div> </div> They were infernalist hollow ones with one kal'shaa for spice. One of them was a widderslante and was a questing (the evil cow was the one who dragged the cabal down.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T01:58:43-07:00","id":1465108,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1229374-1000-rotes?p=1465064#post1465064\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They were infernalist hollow ones with one kal'shaa for spice. One of them was a widderslante and was a questing (the evil cow was the one who dragged the cabal down.)</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the Widderslainte was of the Tormented Essence, right? Remember, the Widderslainte Essences are: Frozen, Tormented, Destruction, Chaotic <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\"><b>Glimpse the Workings</b> [Prime 1, Time 2] - this Rote allows a Mage to sense what Magick Effects another Mage has cast. The Effects are detected from the most recent one, and additional successes have to be allocated to detect and gain information about more Effects. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-size:13px\">Mystics using it on Technocrats and Technomancers, and vice versa, require one additional success to overcome the approach and outlook differences. </span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-28T16:12:36-07:00","id":1465713,"title":"","content":"<b>Earth Bubble</b> [Prime 2, Matter 3, Forces 3] A self-replenishing bubble of fresh air that maintains itself at a comfortable temperature that the caster can push down into the Earth by recasting, allowing a troupe to venture deep underground.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thank you for passing time with me in conversation. <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1480242-horizon-s-wild-and-crazy-homebrew-rules-and-metaplot-choices\" target=\"_blank\">My Hacks</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26467-horizonparty2021","name":"HorizonParty2021","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26467_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-30T09:09:20-07:00","id":1465906,"title":"","content":"<b>City Stride</b> [Correspondence 3] - This Rote makes the Mage able to walk much more quickly through a city, walking through many kilometers long streets as if they were just 100 or 200 meters long. With enough success, entire streets or areas can be skipped as the Mage is focused on the destination. This Rote only works if the Mage has a clear intention of traveling to a visited before area during the cast. For the Rote to be maintained, the Mage must keep going towards the goal without straying from the shortest path; though taking breaks from the travel is acceptable. This Rote only works while traveling on foot - taking a vehicle for transportation ends this Effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-31T05:38:40-07:00","id":1466001,"title":"","content":"<b>Conjure Sensual Phenomena </b>[Prime 2] - This Rote conjures a phenomenon derived from one of the five senses - sight, touch, taste, hearing, smell. This conjuration is more than simply an illusion, though it lasts for at most a minute or two unless additional successes are applied to duration. Conjuring a phenomenon of taste or touch requires specifically targeting a person (or a group), of course.<br /> Mages can conjure a multitude of sensations - a scent of roses and tulips, images of far-away plains and rivers, sounds of careless laughter, a taste of an exquisite supper. or a touch of finest fabrics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-18T04:12:29-08:00","id":1470776,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">Okay, here are copies of a couple of my priest's rotes.<br /> <br /> <b>Rites of the Dead Religion.</b> Rotes for Some Hermetical mages, rare Dream-speakers, some specific religion/spiritual Orphans or Demon's priests. Sisters of Hippolyta - for Zodiacal asylum &amp; Call of Nergal-Kalba (If any of them follow Hellenism).<br /> <i>For obvious reasons, technomages (and pure techno-shamans), Celestial Chorus, Taft\u00e2ni &amp; etc are unable to recreate or use these rites.</i></span></span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>\u00abCall of Nergal-Kalba\u00bb </b> <b>(Spirit \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, optional Entropy \u25cf and / or Prime \u25cf)</b> \u2014 A rite created at the end of the 16th century by the cult of the Hellenistic priests, an old magister-hermeticist and his only disciple. These records are kept in the hidden and inconspicuous Chantry due to the risk of being accused of summoning demons by other magicians. It is an adaptation of the Babylonian rites, partly distorted by the Greek faith. The ritual is needed to attract the demons of Nergal and the self-possession of the magician; optionally, the magician can draw out his life-force to enhance the ritual and give it a connection with death (a feeling of decay / death during the time of possession).<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> The magician summons a demon by the Babylonian-Hellenic rite. At the end of the ceremony, the magician falls under partial control (one of the forms of possession, like bane's fomori) by one of the demons close to the Babylonian faith and the world of the dead (that are able to haunt souls of the dead) or by spectres and very rarely - barghests (ghosts turned into a beasts).<br /> To successfully complete the ritual and summon a weak demon to one scene, the mage needs 5 successes. Additional successes (with the addition of the correct big ceremony) can be spent on extending possession time or to summon a specific/powerful spirit. If desired, the priest can sacrifice himself - they inflict wounds and bleeding on themselves. Using <b>Entropy</b>, the priest focuses on dying and bounding himself with death, beginning to feel decay/ill fate in others (in the form of feeling wounds, illnesses or other events). By adding <b>Prime</b>, the priest can sacrifice his life for the ritual, decreasing the difficulty of the ritual. The priest who uses both spheres reveals the ideal sense of death, seeing how decay affects the environment (selective vision of the aura, mainly focused on the extinction of life and the resonance of death). Depending on the demon, the magician falls under the influence of the spirit and its desires, the body of the magician occasionally receives minor temporary changes. There is a risk of losing control over oneself, then the spirit will guide the magician. Charms or arcanoi remain at the disposal of the spirit and only it can use them at any time during possession.<br /> <br /> <b>Foci:</b> Dagger or curved sword, sacred text, sacrifice</span></span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>\u00abZisurr\u00fb / Zodiacal Asylum\u00bb (Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Spirit \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b> \u2014 Two protective rites. The first ritual (Zisurr\u00fb) is different ritual of the same name that performs the same function. By infusing the power bestowed by the gods into the chosen place, the priest protects the place from demons. The second rite (Zodiacal Asylum) is a complex rite of protection recreated (and changed) from damaged texts by the Hellenistic cult that combined Greek and Sumerian beliefs. This ritual protects a room, a house, and even majestic buildings and fortresses. A small circle and statues of gods are enough to protect a small room. To protect a average temple or fortress, large statues 3 (or more) meters high may be required. The larger the area of protection, the more quintessence will be required and the more complex and detailed the circle needs to be recreated.<br /> <br /> <b>System (Zisurr\u00fb):</b> The priest draws a protective flour circle around the place of sleep and recites an ancient spell (difficulty - 8). This rite protects the place from demons, but every success spent to increase barrier level by 1 requires spending of quintessence; this rite can't protect more than one lunar month (29-30 days) and is not able to raise the barrier above 9 (however, the number of successes required to pass will increase). All sacrificed quintessence becomes a spiritual shield, which increases the difficulty of any attempts to destroy the barrier (works as an anti-magic; optional - separate successes are needed to form the shield).<br /> <br /> <b>System (Zodiacal Asylum):</b> Someone should draw (or better cut out in the material) a zodiacal circle with constellations divided into segments, and also divide the circle (possibly also the ceiling) into 3 \u00abspheres\u00bb of the universe (Upper World - Heaven, Middle World - Earth, Underworld - Irkalla). Statues of gods (syncretic combinations of the Greek and Babylonian gods were often used) must be individually consecrated with the correct rituals (and imbued with their power - by using <b>Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Matter \u25cf\u25cf</b>) or crafted from the correct materials (tass + craft roll; <b>Prime </b>\u25cf to identify the correct material. Over time, such statues will &quot;deplete&quot; and lose their power).<br /> After completing the preparation, the priest (but more often the priests) perform a ceremony at each statue and donate a quintesense or tass to them (preferably with the correct resonance for each statue). The statues will create an aura that will increase the difficulty of any corrupting spiritual powers (as well as suppressing demonic diseases and powers), and even scares away some spirits. Maximum duration of protection for such a circle is also equal to lunar month, but priest doesn't need new statues (if the old ones remain intact). Statues made of tass have a chance of collapsing at the end of the lunar cycle if their quintessence was used in the ritual.<br /> The simplified version (mostly for one room protection) allows priest to use a statue of one god (although a full circle is still needed), but this protection only works during the time period of that zodiac sign.<br /> <br /> <b>Foci</b>: For Zisurr\u00fb \u2014 flour, sleeping place and god's blessing (quintessence); For Zodiacal Asylum \u2014 sacred statues of gods, a zodiac circle built in the correct position relative to the signs (the sign on the floor should be directed to its constellation in the sky, at the right time), a holy place or washed materials (tass), possibly several groups of workers.</span></span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>\u00abWeapon of Destruction\u00bb (</b>Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Spirit \u25cf\u25cf<b>) </b>\u2014 Calling to Nergal seeing his manifestation in heaven (\u1e62albat\u0101nu \u2014 Mars), the priest-warrior can get his favor and protection. For this, the priest sacrifices an animal and inflicts a wound on himself or sprinkles with his blood the copper sacred weapons of the god (a curved sword, mace, wand, dagger). Priest's life go away, bringing him closer to the god, but also grant him the strength to fight the spirits (the weapons are able to attack the spirits). Each success is one turn during which priest can attack demons, but he need to spend at least 1 point of quintessence per turn. </span></span>The ritual creates a flow of quintessence, along the contour of the blood on the weapon, in the spiritual plane.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>Foci: </b>curved sword, mace, wand, dagger</span></span> <hr /><br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b>\u00abUdug-\u1e2bul\u00bb (Spirit \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, optional Mind \u25cf and / or Prime \u25cf) </b>\u2014 An ancient ritual for driving out evil spirits. To drive out the evil udug, the priest turns to the good udug (often asking deities for it before that). The ritual allows the priest to &quot;attach&quot; the spirit to the person, but in the end, the priest cannot force the good spirit and it is free to leave early if it wants to.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> Priest summons the good Udug (spirit / demon) who comes to drive the evil Udug out of the person. To summon the correct spirit, the priest needs a minimum of 2-5 successes. This number of successes varies depending on the patronage of the gods, knowledge of the name of desired spirit, and the power of the evil spirit. On rare occasions, the summoned spirit may be weak and unable to drive out the evil one.<br /> On the other hand, the priest can turn to the gods and ask them for such spirit; perhaps the gods will send spirit. In this case, the priest only needs to establish a connection with the deity, in any correct way (with the help of magic, messenger spirits, direct spiritual connection, etc.). The power of such spirit, as well as debts and consequences, are at the discretion of ST.<br /> Banishment itself differs from others old and modern exorcism in that a good spirit (not priest) drives out an evil spirit and takes its place; it does not take possession of a person, but will patronize him for some time (from a couple of minutes to days; but udug will never protect him more than the lunar cycle).<br /> The addition of <b>Mind </b></span></span><b>\u25cf </b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">allows mage to sense thoughts of possessed person &amp; demon, and <b>Prime </b></span></span><b>\u25cf </b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><span style=\"font-family:arial\">allow to feel the spirit and its nature (reading the shade of spirit resonance).<br /> <br /> <b>Foci:</b> Spell text, kind Udug, connection to the Babylonian / Mesopotamian(?) gods</span></span> <hr /><br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>\u00abThe Phenomenon of Place\u00bb (Spirit/Prime/Entropy \u25cf)</b> \u2014 for the perception / feeling of the spiritual resonance of the place, the priest must stop and create a circle (from a mixture of milk, sand, special herbs; the mixture must be made of materials that have no infernal corruption) covered with symbols of constellations and tune his feelings to </span>surrounding <span style=\"font-size:12px\">flows. Having tuned in, the priest will be able to feel the shade and movement of the flow, getting an idea of \u200b\u200bwhat kind of force circulates in the environment [elemental (fire) / evil (curse) / holy (divine healing in a temple or a good ritual of purification) / chaotic (disincarnation / breakthrough of Wyrm's</span><span style=\"font-size:12px\"> forces into the reality / Storm of the underworld)]<br /> If the materials have been tainted by entropy, the priest will sense his own circle, but on rare occasions he will be able to better see the effects of withering. This entropy ritual is very difficult to read (roll has additional diff modifier +2 and every 2 successes equals 1 success in terms of the information received). If the materials were corrupted by infernal forces, then the priest will feel the presence of this power around him, this will make him believe that the place is in the power of demons / genies / devas. Moreover, any infernal forces will be hidden in a false aura (+ 1-2 to the difficulty of detection) and if they are not corrupted more than material of the circle, they will not be detected by this ritual.<br /> <br /> <b>Foci</b>: powder</span> <hr /><br /> <b>\u00abRevelation\u00bb (Spirit/Life <b>\u25cf</b>)</b> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2014 </span>Revelation allows the priest to feel a spiritual presence that overlaps reality.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>System:</b> </span>The priest reads in his mind a prayer appeal for entering a short trance. In this state, the priest is able to feel (like those who have awareness) the touch of the spirit in our world. This allows the priest to feel the touch of spirits on the living (bonds or remnants of a recent influence), to feel a spiritual presence in people (obsession); feel the echoes of the spirit in its body (when spirits or fairies create a material body for themselves). This power cannot reveal the secrets of these creatures, it only indicates that the spirits were in close contact with a certain creature.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Foci:</b> </span>Trance, prayer <hr /><br /> <b>\u00abWashing/Hiding the Soul</b><b>\u00bb (Mind \u25cf or Prime \u25cf\u25cf or both</b><b>)</b> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2014 </span>[as Shroud the Soul, M20 Fallen p.151] <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2014 </span>The old Greek priests (as well as the seekers of the Sumerian-Akkadian knowledge) taught that demons, ghosts and attentive people can feel fears and thoughts, and they can use them.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>System(</b></span><b>Washing</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>):</b> </span>To protect against manipulation, priest performs washing [<b>Mind \u25cf</b>] that calms mind and removes unnecessary thoughts from the mind (and also suppresses part of his aura). The duration of the effect is limited by the maintained concentration.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>System(</b></span><b>Hiding the Soul</b><span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>):</b> </span>Sometimes priests get negative resonance or their soul has a noticeable distinguishing feature, be it a demon's mark or an echo of carnage. In such cases, the priests perform ritual [<b>Prime \u25cf\u25cf</b>] aimed at hiding the nature of these traces, directing their will to replace them with others (Roll: Will, difficulty resonance + 3 = -1 in resonance for each success). The effect will last no more than an hour, or until the priest does something that could reveal the original mark or destroy its &quot;mask&quot;.<br /> <br /> The combo version clears the mind and hides spiritual traits. The ceremony is complex and lasts no more than an hour, but it allows the priest to hide his soul and mind.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\"><b>Foci:</b> </span>Concentration, water<br /> <hr /> <hr /><br /> Complex of rituals: <b>\u00abIrkalla's Appeals\u00bb (Spirit \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf </b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2014 </span><b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Entropy \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf </b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2014</span><b> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, optional Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2014 </span>a list of rituals for interacting with the underworld and the demons living there.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>\u00abDeath of Inanna\u00bb (Spirit \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Entropy \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2014 </span>The priest performs in a place (room, street, grave) a rite with the participation of objects similar or copying the \u00abInanna's Seven Secret Powers\u00bb (a representation of a powerful <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Me_(mythology)\" target=\"_blank\">me </a>she possessed). The priest of the rite conducts a ceremony honoring and telling about the sacrifice of Inanna, her departure to Irkalla and her subsequent return. Completing the ceremony, the priest can call the departed soul into the world of the living, but in return he must offer himself. An important aspect of the ritual is going to Irkalla, for which the priest needs to injure himself. Often the ritual ends with hanging the mutilated body on hooks <b>[and losing at least 5 health blocks]</b>.<br /> <br /> The success of the ritual will lead to the fall of the ghost of the priest (who becomes an ordinary ghost) to the area closest to the world of the living, and the summoned ghost will appear at the place of the ritual (which does not guarantee its visibility to others).<br /> So it is impossible to call souls captive outside Irkalla or located in its depths or the Storm. Also, due to the fact that Irkalla cannot <b><i>\u00abjust\u00bb</i></b> be left, the priest is obliged to sacrifice something of his own (temporary will in the amount of 3 or more; valuable thing, friend...), if the sacrifice turns out to be incomplete, the world will take the difference in the form of (permanent) Will, his mystical powers (will put a part of the avatar to sleep; Or, if he used more powerful rites, put the priest before the Torment [Harrowing]).<br /> <hr /><br /> If the priest has attained the greatest spiritual secrets <b>Spirit </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - he can learn the complex <b>\u00abRite of the Seventh Gate\u00bb (Spirit </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf<b>, Entropy \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf</b><b>)</b> dedicated to the conflict between Inanna and Ereshkigal; then he can offer his body (if the spirit has the power to possess), help the ghost to get into his body, or forcibly shackle in his body. If successful, the spirit takes over the crippled (but possibly treatable) body, it can feel and has limited control. The Ghost does not become Risen and cannot heal wounds on its own.<br /> <hr /><br /> Priests who know the <b>Entropy</b> \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf can memorize the <b>\u00abGift to the Gatekeeper\u00bb (Spirit \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Entropy \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf) </b><span style=\"font-size:12px\">\u2014</span> rite dedicated to Nergal. Only this rite, in which <i>\u201c10 first-class, fat, ritually clean sheep, whose horn and nail are not damaged\u201d</i> are sacrificed, is able to open the gates to almost any place in Irkalla. This allows priest to summon ghosts and specters who have gone into the depths (although, those whom the priest did not call are often called back). Also, few of the priests spoke of other creatures living in that world that are similar to beasts, demons, or <i>&quot;unseen before&quot;</i>; some managed to call, albeit not for long, it is obvious that these are the servants of Nergal.<br /> By combining the <b>\u00abGift to the Gatekeeper\u00bb</b> with the <b>Spirit </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, the priest (who brought even more sacrifices from pure creatures) is able to briefly open a passage for the demons of Nergal or the souls of the dead. These entities do not obey the priest and are free to do what they want, in the end, the priest asks only to let them go for a while.<br /> <hr /><br /> Mastering <b>Entropy </b>and <b>Spirit </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf allows spiritually enlightened priests to perform the <b>\u00abSeventh Gate\u00bb</b> and <b>\u00abDeath of Inanna\u00bb</b> rituals bloodlessly. The priest gradually breaks the bonds that bind the soul. The priest <b>must</b> inflict important injuries (hanging on hooks), but he is able to descend into Irkalla on his own. But this descent takes the priest's soul closer to the Storm and depths of the Underworld - where he will almost certainly be harrowing.<br /> <br /> Having approached the divine and having mastered the <b>Entropy </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, the priest can use ideas as a sacrifice (instead of health, quintessence, will or things) in the <b>\u00abSeventh Gate\u00bb</b> and <b>\u00abDeath of Inanna\u00bb</b> rituals. Irkalla's call will erase him from someone else's life (or erase his memories; however, both options can happen).<br /> <br /> <b>Prime </b>\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf is needed to collect the outgoing life and direct the sacrifice to the object of the ritual. The priest performing the rituals of Inanna can risk and offer his life as a sacrifice<i> (1 quintessence point per health block)</i>, this will create a shroud of wind and dust that will protect the priest from the Storm and ghosts (The Storyteller's Job; simply creates a ghost shroud passing into chains). Such wounds cannot be healed by ordinary methods and rituals, and the priest runs the risk of leaving on himself the stigma of the Afterlife (Example: illness, loss of fertility, scars).<br /> <br /> The priest of Nergal can direct the outgoing life of the sheep <b>(Prime \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf, Entropy \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf - \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</b> into the Kingdom of the Dead to God or his intermediary, which helps to strengthen the rite. Such a sacrifice allows for additional successes to extend the existence of the passage to Irkalla by 1 turn for each point of sacrificial quintessence or to reduce the difficulty for summoning a ghost from Irkalla. It is also possible to attract the ghosts or demons of Irkalla, if the resonance and form of quintessence suits them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25408,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","user":"Alphari","date":". 01-04-2022, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25408-alphari","name":"Alphari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25408_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"153"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-01T08:41:15-08:00","id":1471593,"title":"","content":"Anull Luck [Entropy 2] - This relatively simple Rote ensures that the target wilk not be benefitting from a spree of beneficial occurances, whether natural or magickly induced. This has great utility in stopping a rampage in a combat situation, as well as a lucky spree in a casino, or during a card game or a board game session played for fun. Whatever the situation, This Rote subdues an above average show of luck into a mediocre or unsatisfactory outcome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 01-07-2022, 01:11 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}